#  ***************************************************************************
#  Lumped companion to project_tet10_dyn (GitHub issue #11 + the lumped
#  recovery path). Same dynamic Tet<10> cube and every-step write, but with
#  "Mass Matrix Type: Lumped".
#
#  A lumped projection is a mass-weighted nodal average, so it does NOT
#  reproduce a linear field exactly -- proj_nodal_linear is checked relative
#  against the gold rather than absolute. The regression it guards is still
#  GitHub #11: if the first computed frame's projected fields drop to zero,
#  they differ from the gold's non-zero lumped values and the diff fails.
#  ***************************************************************************

COORDINATES absolute 1.e-6

TIME STEPS relative 1.e-6 floor 0.0

NODAL VARIABLES relative 1.0e-5 floor 1.0e-9

ELEMENT VARIABLES relative 1.0e-5 floor 1.0e-8
